# ==============================================================================
# REBUILD V4 — byte-stability for generated CSVs (appended; nothing above changed).
# pandas writes CRLF on Windows, and core.autocrlf normalises it to LF on commit, so
# the on-disk bytes of every generated CSV differed from its own blob. A clean clone
# therefore got different INPUT bytes than the tree they were produced in, and the
# clean-clone check compared files that could never match. Worse, these CSVs carry
# embedded newlines inside quoted free-text fields (incident_details), where the
# rewrite is not a harmless line-ending change.
#
# Scoped to v4 paths ONLY. v3 blobs must not be renormalised: scripts/210 compares
# them byte for byte.
# ==============================================================================
outputs/essay3_v4/**/*.csv -text
outputs/rebuild_v4/**/*.csv -text
Data/processed/rebuild_v4/**/*.csv -text

